<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 154,400 tonnes wheat, 77,500 t barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 154,400 tonnes wheat, 77,500 t barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 74,400 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Australian wheat, and 37,500 tonnes of Canadian barley and 40,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender, all for February shipment.</p>
<p>Japan also bought 5,600 tonnes of American hull-less barley and 2,500 tonnes of Canadian hull-less barley.</p>
<p>This is the last tender by the Japan's Food Agency for calendar 1996.</p>
<p>Details of the tender results are as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	  74,400	  Western white	    25,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter	  20,000</p>
<p>				   Ordinary		   15,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern	    14,400</p>
<p> Canada	40,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  40,000</p>
<p> Australia   40,000	 Standard white	    20,000</p>
<p>				  Prime hard		  20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Canada	37,500	  Feed			 37,500</p>
<p> Australia   40,000	  Feed			 34,000</p>
<p>				   Food			  6,000</p>
<p>HULL-LESS BARLEY</p>
<p> America	5,600</p>
<p> Canada	 2,500</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
